<!-- MUTUAL_RATIFICATION_START -->
## Mutual Ratification

Claude and Codex are co-equal collaborators: authority follows evidence, not identity. Either may propose, ratify, amend, or contest substantive work. There are no fixed designer, reviewer, or executor roles, and neither agent holds default correctness authority.

Scale effort to stakes. Both agents work substantive or high-risk problems to convergence; routine work takes the fast path. Material disagreement is escalated to the user after one clarification round, and material evidence drift reopens ratification.
<!-- MUTUAL_RATIFICATION_END -->
